    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d777">

                <pb facs="1106" n="1614" xml:id="pg1614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/11–1948: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to Certain Diplomatic and Consular Offices
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d777-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-19T18:00:00-05:00">November 19,
                            1948—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    GA plenary session today approved resolution
                    originally submitted by US, UK, Belgium, Netherlands for 32 million dollar
                    program relief Palestinian refugees of all communities covering period ending
                    Aug 31, 1949. Resolution as approved includes 5 million dollar advance from UN
                    working capital fund.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d777-f2"/> Details will follow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d777-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d777-f1-content">
                <p>At Arab capitals, Jerusalem, and Tel Aviv.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d777-f2" n="2" xml:id="d777-f2-content">
                <p>For text of resolution 212(III), see GA, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">3rd sess., Pt. I, Resolutions, 1948</hi>, p. 66.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
